{:edb/db-before-t 2679 :edb/db-after-t 2680 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535992 50 #inst "2026-10-09T12:27:37.690Z" 13194139535992 true] [17592186179477 1100 "Calculate $\\nabla \\cdot (\\mathbf{F}-3\\mathbf{G})$ for the vector fields $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$, where\n$\\mathbf{F}=\\left(x^2+y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+ \\left(xy-y^2\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}, \\quad \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{G}=x+y$." 13194139535992 false] [17592186179477 1100 "Calculate $\\nabla \\cdot (\\mathbf{F}-3\\mathbf{G})$ for the vector fields $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G,$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}=\\left(x^2+y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+ \\left(xy-y^2\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}, \\quad \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{G}=x+y.\n$$" 13194139535992 true] [17592186179477 1145 "If $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $\\nabla \\cdot (k \\mathbf F) = k \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf F$\n\n- $\\nabla \\cdot (\\mathbf F + \\mathbf G) = \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf F + \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-3G) & =∇\\cdot (F)+∇\\cdot (-3G) \\\\  & =∇\\cdot F-3∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{F}.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2x+x-2y \\\\  & =3x-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-3G) & =∇\\cdot F-3∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =(3x-2y)-3\\cdot (x+y) \\\\  & =-5y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535992 true] [17592186179477 1145 "If $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $\\nabla \\cdot (k \\mathbf F) = k \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf F$\n- $\\nabla \\cdot (\\mathbf F + \\mathbf G) = \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf F + \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot (F - 3G) &= ∇ \\cdot (F) + ∇ \\cdot (-3G) \\\\\n&= ∇ \\cdot F - 3∇ \\cdot G\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{F}$. In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot F &= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2} + y) + \\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy - y^{2}) \\\\\n&= 2x + x - 2y \\\\\n&= 3x - 2y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot (F - 3G) &= ∇ \\cdot F - 3∇ \\cdot G \\\\\n&= (3x - 2y) - 3 \\cdot (x + y) \\\\\n&=-5y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535992 false] [17592186179479 1100 "Given that $\\mathbf F(x,y) = \\left\\langle \\dfrac 1x, xy \\right \\rangle$ and $f(x,y) = \\dfrac 1{x}$, calculate $\\nabla \\cdot (f\\,\\mathbf F)$." 13194139535992 false] [17592186179479 1100 "Given that $\\mathbf F(x,y) = \\left\\langle \\dfrac 1x, xy \\right \\rangle$ and $f(x,y) = \\dfrac 1{x},$ calculate $\\nabla \\cdot (f\\,\\mathbf F).$" 13194139535992 true] [17592186179479 1145 "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\nabla \\cdot (f\\,\\mathbf F) = f\\, \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf {F}+  \\mathbf F \\cdot \\nabla f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf {F}$ and $\\nabla f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},0⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+x)+⟨\\frac{1}{x},xy⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},0⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535992 true] [17592186179479 1145 "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\nabla \\cdot (f\\,\\mathbf F) = f\\, \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf {F}+ \\mathbf F \\cdot \\nabla f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf {F}$ and $\\nabla f$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇f &= ⟨ - \\frac{1}{x^{2}}, 0⟩, \\\\\n∇ \\cdot F &= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{x}) + \\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy) =-\\frac{1}{x^{2}} + x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot (fF) &= f∇ \\cdot F + F \\cdot ∇f \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{x}(-\\frac{1}{x^{2}} + x) + ⟨\\frac{1}{x}, xy⟩ \\cdot ⟨ - \\frac{1}{x^{2}}, 0⟩ \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{x^{3}} + 1 - \\frac{1}{x^{3}} \\\\\n&= 1 - \\frac{2}{x^{3}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535992 false] [17592186179618 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378542 13194139535992 true] [17592186179618 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378549 13194139535992 true] [17592186179618 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378556 13194139535992 true] [17592186179618 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378563 13194139535992 true] [17592186179620 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378570 13194139535992 true] [17592186179620 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378577 13194139535992 true] [17592186179620 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378584 13194139535992 true] [17592186179620 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378591 13194139535992 true] [17592186179840 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535992 true] [17592186179840 1100 "Calculate $∇ \\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}F)$ for the vector field $F$ where\n\n$F = xe^{2x}i - ye^{2x}j + xz^{2}k$." 13194139535992 false] [17592186179840 1100 "Calculate $∇\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}F)$ for the vector field $F$ where\n\n$$\nF=x{e}^{2x}\\,i-y{e}^{2x}\\,j+x{z}^{2}\\,k.\n$$" 13194139535992 true] [17592186179840 1145 "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}F)=\\frac{1}{2}∇\\cdot F.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{2x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-y{e}^{2x})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{z}^{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}+2x{e}^{2x}-{e}^{2x}+2xz \\\\  & =2x{e}^{2x}+2xz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}F) & =\\frac{1}{2}∇\\cdot F \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (2x{e}^{2x}+2xz) \\\\  & =x{e}^{2x}+xz.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535992 true] [17592186179841 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535992 true] [17592186179841 1100 "Given that $F(x, y, z) = ⟨e^{3x},-2ye^{3x}⟩$ and $f(x, y) = 2x$, calculate $∇ \\cdot (fF)$." 13194139535992 false] [17592186179841 1100 "Given that $F(x,y,z)=⟨{e}^{3x},-2y{e}^{3x}⟩$ and $f(x,y)=2x,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" 13194139535992 true] [17592186179841 1145 "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨2,0⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{3x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2y{e}^{3x})=3{e}^{3x}-2{e}^{3x}={e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =2x({e}^{3x})+⟨{e}^{3x},-2y{e}^{3x}⟩\\cdot ⟨2,0⟩ \\\\  & =2x{e}^{3x}+2{e}^{3x} \\\\  & =2(x+1){e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378542 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378543 13194139535992 true] [17592186378542 1089 "q-105635" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378542 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535992 true] [17592186378542 1100 "Calculate $∇\\cdot (F-2G)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF={x}^{2}y\\,i+{y}^{2}\\,j,\\,∇\\cdot G=xy+{y}^{2}\n$$" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378542 1113 #uuid "6b6a087b-2c36-534b-953d-ce05fe481ed8" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378542 1145 "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-2G) & =∇\\cdot F-∇\\cdot (2G) \\\\  & =∇\\cdot F-2∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2xy+2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-2G) & =∇\\cdot F-2∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =2xy+2y-2\\cdot (xy+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2xy+2y-2xy-2{y}^{2} \\\\  & =2y-2{y}^{2} \\\\  & =2y(1-y).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378543 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378544 13194139535992 true] [17592186378543 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378545 13194139535992 true] [17592186378543 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378546 13194139535992 true] [17592186378543 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378547 13194139535992 true] [17592186378543 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378548 13194139535992 true] [17592186378543 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535992 true] [17592186378543 1041 "selection" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378543 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378544 13194139535992 true] [17592186378543 1110 #uuid "9e7a25ad-d783-5194-8af2-5226b5ab2e86" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378544 1034 "2y(1-y)" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378544 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535992 true] [17592186378544 1111 #uuid "3f02a394-2462-5fd1-bca8-aecdfca17dc9" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378545 1034 "2y(1+2x+y)" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378545 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535992 true] [17592186378545 1111 #uuid "02a58f04-c260-5017-8312-72da3f94efa4" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378546 1034 "y(2+{y}^{2})" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378546 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535992 true] [17592186378546 1111 #uuid "87aa8f2a-cd34-5e07-bf08-639b02ce5911" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378547 1034 "y(2+x-y)" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378547 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535992 true] [17592186378547 1111 #uuid "c6077cff-b2a2-5f8f-a1a4-21ebd2b52da6" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378548 1034 "y(1-{y}^{2})" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378548 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535992 true] [17592186378548 1111 #uuid "5d1bd6f5-b0e5-587b-ab7e-bc2bd95d7b1c" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378549 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378550 13194139535992 true] [17592186378549 1089 "q-105640" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378549 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535992 true] [17592186378549 1100 "Calculate $∇\\cdot (2F+G)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF={e}^{5x}\\,i+y{e}^{3y}\\,j,\\,∇\\cdot G=3{e}^{5x}-2{e}^{3y}.\n$$" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378549 1113 #uuid "27fbdc78-f989-5a5c-ad92-84d3cb59b67e" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378549 1145 "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (2F+G) & =∇\\cdot (2F)+∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =2∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{5x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{3y}) \\\\  & =5{e}^{5x}+{e}^{3y}+3y{e}^{3y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (2F+G) & =2∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =2\\cdot (5{e}^{5x}+{e}^{3y}+3y{e}^{3y})+3{e}^{5x}-2{e}^{3y} \\\\  & =10{e}^{5x}+2{e}^{3y}+6y{e}^{3y}+3{e}^{5x}-2{e}^{3y} \\\\  & =13{e}^{5x}+6y{e}^{3y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378550 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378551 13194139535992 true] [17592186378550 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378552 13194139535992 true] [17592186378550 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378553 13194139535992 true] [17592186378550 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378554 13194139535992 true] [17592186378550 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378555 13194139535992 true] [17592186378550 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535992 true] [17592186378550 1041 "selection" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378550 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378555 13194139535992 true] [17592186378550 1110 #uuid "f4ac7694-1767-588c-b12d-f501fe4f9050" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378551 1034 "7{e}^{5x}+3{e}^{3y}" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378551 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535992 true] [17592186378551 1111 #uuid "1d8b7c48-14a3-58ea-9de0-a780cb2fa5ed" 13194139535992 true] [17592186378552 1034 "7{e}^{5x}-